  "enable": "AV 47 Demand Enable and AV 48 Tank Setpoint are the writable objects for control; BI 2 BMS Enable reads back the BMS enable input. The guide does not describe the values or the order to write them.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": "AV 49 0-10V BMS Input lets the BMS supply the analog input value; the guide does not say how it is scaled.",
  "setup": [
   "ProtoNode FPC-N54 to the unit: Modbus RTU, 19200 baud, no parity, 8 data bits, 1 stop bit.",
   "Give each unit a unique Node-ID (1-255). BACnet device instance = Node_Offset (default 50,000) + Node-ID.",
   "The BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP field protocol is chosen in the ProtoNode web configurator; default IP 192.168.1.24."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "Access is inferred: the table has no read/write column; AVs (N2 AO) are treated as writable.",
   "Units Present/In Run/In Blocking/In Lockout come as four packed words each, covering units 1-64.",
   "Objects 11-13 are named after raw Modbus registers (30001-30003); their meaning is not given."
  ]
 },
